# This codebase implements the machine-learning pipeline of:
#
#   Alinasab, N., Mohammadzadeh, N., Karimi, A., Mohammadzadeh, R., & Gál, T. (2025).
#   A measurement-based framework integrating machine learning and morphological
#   dynamics for outdoor thermal regulation.
#   International Journal of Biometeorology, 69(9), 1645-1662.
#   https://doi.org/10.1007/s00484-025-02921-8
#
# Code author: Alireza Karimi (University of Stuttgart, IBBTE)

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software (this repository)
  and the original paper it implements.
title: TabrizOTC-ML - Morphology-Driven Outdoor Thermal Comfort Classification
authors:
  - family-names: Karimi
    given-names: Alireza
    affiliation: Institute of Building Materials, Building Physics, Building Technology and Design (IBBTE), University of Stuttgart
  - family-names: Alinasab
    given-names: Niloufar
    affiliation: Department of Atmospheric and Geospatial Data Sciences, University of Szeged
  - family-names: Mohammadzadeh
    given-names: Negar
    affiliation: Department of Architecture, Tarbiat Modares University
  - family-names: Mohammadzadeh
    given-names: Rahmat
    affiliation: Department of Architecture and Urban Design, University of Tabriz
  - family-names: Gál
    given-names: Tamás
    affiliation: Department of Atmospheric and Geospatial Data Sciences, University of Szeged
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-25"
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/Alirezza18/tabriz-otc-ml
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of the machine-learning pipeline from Alinasab et
  al. (2025), Int. J. Biometeorology 69:1645-1662 (DOI
  10.1007/s00484-025-02921-8). Six Bayesian-optimized classifiers (KNN,
  Decision Tree, SVM, Random Forest, XGBoost, CatBoost) predict three outdoor
  thermal comfort indices (UTCI, PET, PMV) from street morphology, followed by
  SHAP interpretation. Ships a synthetic benchmark calibrated to the paper's
  Table 1 feature ranges and Table 2 class fractions; the original field
  measurements are available from the corresponding author on request.
keywords:
  - outdoor thermal comfort
  - machine learning
  - Bayesian optimization
  - SHAP
  - urban climate
  - UTCI
  - PET
  - PMV
  - urban morphology
